Imports:
  - Types:
      - TSGroupThread
    From: SignalServiceKit/Threads

Usages:
  stateless_facade_mutation: |
    Group mutation is not modeled as methods on a stateful group object; a single generic
    mutation entry point accepts a block that describes the desired change, applies it against
    the group's current server-side state, and persists the resulting model. Nearly every
    specific mutation (renaming, membership changes, access changes) is implemented as a thin
    wrapper around this one generic entry point.
  snapshot_then_diff: |
    Remote group state is always fetched as a full, versioned snapshot at a given revision;
    local persistence reconciles the new snapshot against the previously persisted model by
    diffing, rather than applying incremental deltas blindly.

Annotations: |
  This cell owns creation, mutation, and persistence of group conversations: translating
  local mutation intents into server-side group-protocol changes, and reconciling
  server-reported group state into the locally persisted group model and its thread.
  Use `stateless_facade_mutation` for `GroupManager`.
  Use `snapshot_then_diff` for `GroupsV2`'s snapshot-fetching behavior.
  Use `TSGroupThread` from Imports as the thread type every persisted group is backed by.

---

"GroupManager()":
  location: GroupManager.swift
  annotations: |
    Stateless static facade orchestrating every local and remote group mutation.

    Use `stateless_facade_mutation` for the overall mutation algorithm.
    Use `TSGroupThread` from Imports as the return type of group creation/lookup.
  methods:
    "localCreateNewGroup(members: [String], name: String, avatarData: Data?) -> groupThread: TSGroupThread": |
      Creates a new group on the server and persists the resulting group thread locally.

      `members`: initial member addresses
      `name`: initial group title
    "updateGroupAttributes(title: String?, description: String?, avatarData: Data?, inExistingGroup: TSGroupThread)": |
      Changes a group's title, description, and/or avatar.

      Algorithm:
      1. Build a change block describing the requested attribute changes.
      2. Apply it via the generic mutation entry point per `stateless_facade_mutation`.
      3. Persist the resulting updated group model and insert an info message describing the change.
    "addOrInvite(groupThread: TSGroupThread, serviceIds: [String])": |
      Adds or invites the given members to an existing group, depending on the group's access
      settings.
    "localLeaveGroupOrDeclineInvite(groupThread: TSGroupThread, tx: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Removes the local user from the group, or declines a pending invitation to it.

"GroupsV2()":
  location: GroupsV2.swift
  annotations: |
    Protocol abstracting the group server-protocol boundary: fetching and mutating
    server-side group state.

    Use `snapshot_then_diff` for how snapshots are fetched and reconciled.
  methods:
    "createNewGroupOnService(members: [String]) -> snapshotResponse: String": |
      Creates a new group on the server and returns its initial snapshot.
    "fetchLatestSnapshot(secretParams: Data) -> snapshotResponse: String": |
      Fetches the current server-side state of a group at its latest revision.
    "updateGroupV2(secretParams: Data, changesBlock: String) -> results: [String]": |
      Applies a described set of changes to a group on the server.

      `changesBlock`: describes the requested change, per `stateless_facade_mutation`

"GroupMembership()":
  location: GroupMembership.swift
  annotations: |
    Immutable value object describing the full/invited/requesting/banned membership state of
    one group, and the role of each full member.
  methods:
    "isFullMember(address: String) -> isMember: Bool": |
      Returns whether the given address is currently a full (non-invited, non-requesting)
      member.
    "role(address: String) -> role: String?": |
      Returns the given member's role (administrator or ordinary member), if they are a member.

"TSGroupModelV2()":
  location: TSGroupModel.swift
  annotations: |
    The persisted, versioned model of one group's attributes, membership, and access settings,
    mirrored one-to-one with its `TSGroupThread`.
  properties:
    "revision -> Int": |
      The server-side revision number this locally persisted model reflects.
    "descriptionText -> String?": |
      The group's optional description text.
    "isTerminated -> Bool": |
      Whether the group has been terminated (e.g. all members removed by an admin action).

